{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115718",
      "title": "Using The viewChild Signal Function",
      "lectureOrder": 133,
      "videoOrder": 127,
      "sourceHash": "649fd6b463d7b158a5520f6a11dfc032e000f0ec77db24d47d02c7f29cefcb3e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.781,
          "end": 3.72,
          "en": "So ViewChild is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.72,
          "end": 6.87,
          "en": "There also is ViewChildren,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.87,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "if you wanted to select multiple elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 13.74,
          "en": "For example, if I had multiple custom buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.74,
          "end": 16.95,
          "en": "in that template, we could use ViewChildren",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.95,
          "end": 19.11,
          "en": "with the button component like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 22.35,
          "en": "to in the end store an array of buttons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.35,
          "end": 25.14,
          "en": "in this property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.14,
          "end": 28.26,
          "en": "or an array of ElementRefs that will resolve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.26,
          "end": 31.623,
          "en": "to my button component instances, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.64,
          "end": 37.64,
          "en": "So ViewChildren is an important variation of ViewChild,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.83,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "you could say, in case you need to select",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "multiple ViewChild items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 46.17,
          "en": "Another important variation is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.17,
          "end": 48.72,
          "en": "besides using it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.72,
          "end": 52.353,
          "en": "you can also use ViewChild as a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.28,
          "end": 57.88,
          "en": "So you could add a potentially private form property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 63.8,
          "en": "and we could have marked this here as private as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.58,
          "end": 66.693,
          "en": "Let's maybe do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 67.59,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "But instead of doing that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 71.22,
          "en": "we could also create a property like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 71.22,
          "end": 74.25,
          "en": "without the ViewChild decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.25,
          "end": 77.643,
          "en": "and instead call viewChild as a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 79.56,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "And for that you must import the viewChild function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 84.003,
          "en": "from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 86.1,
          "end": 89.76,
          "en": "Now, the viewChild function is a relatively new feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 89.76,
          "end": 93.72,
          "en": "it's only been available since Angular 17.3",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 93.72,
          "end": 98.22,
          "en": "and it's not available in older Angular versions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 98.22,
          "end": 103.22,
          "en": "And viewChild will actually give you a Signal as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.95,
          "end": 106.77000000000001,
          "en": "So it's a Signal-related feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.77000000000001,
          "end": 110.64,
          "en": "Now it generally works like the decorator though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 110.64,
          "end": 113.49199999999999,
          "en": "You pass a selector to viewChild,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 113.49199999999999,
          "end": 116.55,
          "en": "like the ButtonComponent class name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 120,
          "en": "If you wanted to select a button in your template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 120,
          "end": 125,
          "en": "a custom ButtonComponent occurrence in your template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "or a string with a template variable name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 131.553,
          "en": "if you wanna select an element by template variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 133.53,
          "end": 136.62,
          "en": "So that would then give us hold of a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 136.62,
          "end": 141.03300000000002,
          "en": "that in the end resolves to our HTML form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 142.11,
          "end": 143.73,
          "en": "Though, as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 143.73,
          "end": 146.55,
          "en": "if you hover over form, Angular doesn't know that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.55,
          "end": 148.71,
          "en": "It just knows that it will be a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 148.71,
          "end": 151.65,
          "en": "with a unknown value, and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 151.65,
          "end": 154.23,
          "en": "just as with ViewChild up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 154.23,
          "end": 158.82,
          "en": "you also have to give Angular or specifically TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 162,
          "en": "some extra type information here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 162,
          "end": 165.27,
          "en": "And you should let TypeScript know which kind of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.27,
          "end": 167.52,
          "en": "will be stored in form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.52,
          "end": 171.09,
          "en": "or will be stored in that Signal here in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 171.09,
          "end": 173.97,
          "en": "And you do that by adding angle brackets again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 173.97,
          "end": 177.6,
          "en": "because if viewChild is again such a generic type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 180.15,
          "en": "which creates a Signal that works together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 180.15,
          "end": 182.43,
          "en": "with other type values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 182.43,
          "end": 186.81,
          "en": "the types of the values stored in it, to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.81,
          "end": 189.48,
          "en": "and the type of values stored in that Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 189.48,
          "end": 192.54,
          "en": "will again be an ElementRef object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 192.54,
          "end": 197.54,
          "en": "which then internally stores such a HTML form element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 198.51,
          "end": 201.18,
          "en": "And with that you can then use this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201.18,
          "end": 204.9,
          "en": "and execute it as a function because it's a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 204.9,
          "end": 207.933,
          "en": "and then access nativeElement.reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 209.07,
          "end": 211.95,
          "en": "Now as you can see, I'm getting an error here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 211.95,
          "end": 214.59300000000002,
          "en": "that the object is possibly undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 215.64,
          "end": 218.88,
          "en": "because indeed if you hover over this form property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.88,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "you can see that the Signal that is produced by Angular here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 225.18,
          "en": "will give us such a ElementRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 225.18,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "which then internally holds this FormElement object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 232.38,
          "en": "But alternatively it could also give us undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 232.38,
          "end": 236.433,
          "en": "if it fails to find that element somewhere in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 237.54,
          "end": 240.6,
          "en": "Now what we can do again is use this question mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.6,
          "end": 245.07,
          "en": "to tell TypeScript and Angular and JavaScript in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 245.07,
          "end": 248.22,
          "en": "that we only want to execute all this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.22,
          "end": 253.22,
          "en": "if this.form Signal does hold such a ElementRef object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 253.35,
          "end": 257.67,
          "en": "Alternatively, there also is an alternative version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 257.67,
          "end": 260.7,
          "en": "of that viewChild function, which you could use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.7,
          "end": 263.91,
          "en": "and that's the required function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 263.91,
          "end": 267.93,
          "en": "So on the viewChild function, you ask the required function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 267.93,
          "end": 270.63,
          "en": "or the required method actually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 270.63,
          "end": 273.81,
          "en": "which also selects an element in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 273.81,
          "end": 275.31,
          "en": "with help of that selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 275.31,
          "end": 278.67,
          "en": "but which, unlike viewChild without required,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 278.67,
          "end": 282.213,
          "en": "guarantees that an element will be found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 283.08,
          "end": 285.45,
          "en": "And therefore, of course, you must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 285.45,
          "end": 290.45,
          "en": "that you do have a selector here that will yield an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 291.12,
          "end": 294.12,
          "en": "so that you don't use a selector here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 294.12,
          "end": 297.36,
          "en": "that wouldn't produce an element like forms,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 297.36,
          "end": 299.97,
          "en": "then you would run into issues.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 299.97,
          "end": 302.88,
          "en": "So that's something you have to check for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 302.88,
          "end": 307.71,
          "en": "But here with form, I know that this form will always exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 307.71,
          "end": 310.77,
          "en": "and that it can be found in the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 310.77,
          "end": 313.74,
          "en": "and therefore I can use this required version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 313.74,
          "end": 316.2,
          "en": "of the viewChild function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 316.2,
          "end": 319.47,
          "en": "so that Angular and TypeScript in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 319.47,
          "end": 323.97,
          "en": "knows that this form property will always hold a Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 323.97,
          "end": 327.24,
          "en": "that will always produce such a ElementRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 327.24,
          "end": 330.39,
          "en": "that will hold the FormElement object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 330.39,
          "end": 334.92,
          "en": "And that's then that Signal way of resetting that form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 334.92,
          "end": 337.353,
          "en": "with help of that viewChild function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 338.31,
          "end": 340.86,
          "en": "which, besides giving us a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 340.86,
          "end": 344.97,
          "en": "also allows us to avoid this ViewChild decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 344.97,
          "end": 347.13,
          "en": "And if you're not a fan of decorators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 347.13,
          "end": 348.99,
          "en": "that therefore might be another reason",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 348.99,
          "end": 351.36,
          "en": "for using that function instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 351.36,
          "end": 353.7,
          "en": "But, as mentioned, it's only available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 353.7,
          "end": 358.38,
          "en": "if you're using Angular 17.3 or newer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 358.38,
          "end": 361.71,
          "en": "With that, however, if I enter something here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 361.71,
          "end": 365.853,
          "en": "and I submit this, you see that form is reset again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 366.99,
          "end": 368.85,
          "en": "And, of course, it's also worth noting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 368.85,
          "end": 371.22,
          "en": "that besides this viewChild function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 371.22,
          "end": 374.52,
          "en": "there also is a viewChildren function in case you need it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 374.52,
          "end": 377.793,
          "en": "to select multiple elements in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 378.9,
          "end": 380.58299999999997,
          "en": "We don't need that here though.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
